3. Return M
```

G.3 Proof

Theorem G.1 (Extraction consistency). Under the assumptions of Theorem F.1 and the faithfulness of the causal graph, Algorithm G.1 returns the set of minimal subgraphs satisfying Definition 3.6 with probability tending to 1 as N \to \infty.

Proof. By Theorem F.1, O_{\mathrm{causal}} is identified. The downstream subgraph test is a conditional independence test: m is causally downstream of O_{\mathrm{causal}} if m \perp O_{\mathrm{non-causal}} \mid O_{\mathrm{causal}}. This test is consistent under faithfulness. Recursion terminates because A is finite and acyclic. Definition 3.6 criteria 1–4 are verified by interventional contrasts, which are consistent by Theorem A.1. \square

